WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.156
The intelligence lifecycle turns a broad concern into a repeatable analytical process.

00:00:06.156 --> 00:00:16.873
It begins with requirements: the specific questions the work must answer, the decision it will support, the permitted scope, and the deadline.

00:00:16.873 --> 00:00:22.118
Clear requirements prevent endless collection and reduce unnecessary privacy impact.

00:00:22.118 --> 00:00:27.362
Collection identifies and obtains relevant public material using approved methods.

00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:34.430
A collection plan maps each requirement to likely source categories, priorities, and stopping conditions.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:41.043
Analysts should avoid gathering sensitive personal information simply because it is technically visible.

00:00:41.043 --> 00:00:45.375
Processing converts collected material into a usable form.

00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:55.180
This may include organizing records, normalizing dates, extracting text from permitted documents, translating content, removing duplicates, and preserving source metadata.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.056
Processing should not erase provenance or uncertainty.

00:00:59.056 --> 00:01:04.301
Analysis compares observations, tests explanations, identifies patterns, and assesses significance.

00:01:04.301 --> 00:01:09.089
Validation checks source origin, timing, internal consistency, and corroboration.

00:01:09.089 --> 00:01:17.526
Analysts should actively look for disconfirming evidence instead of selecting only material that supports an early theory.

00:01:17.526 --> 00:01:21.402
Reporting communicates findings for the intended audience.

00:01:21.402 --> 00:01:30.750
A useful report answers the requirement, cites supporting evidence, distinguishes fact from inference, states confidence, and identifies important gaps.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:36.451
Detail should match the reader's role and the consequences of action.

00:01:36.451 --> 00:01:38.959
Feedback closes the lifecycle.

00:01:38.959 --> 00:01:44.659
Decision-makers may refine the requirement, request clarification, or identify new questions.

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:50.360
Analysts can also improve source selection and documentation based on review.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:57.428
The lifecycle is iterative, but it remains bounded by purpose, authority, time, and proportionality.
